-- title:
--   Orbit–stabiliser count for level automorphisms at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a field $L$ the Laurent series field $L((T))$ carries the operator `qExpand L d`, substitution $T \mapsto T^{d}$, and the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb L` of $\mathbb Q((T))$ into $L((T))$. A place of $F$ over $K$ (the structure `Place`) is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `ord` is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, `IsRational` says that $K$ surjects onto the residue field of the place, and `evalAt f` is the preimage in $K$ of the residue of $f$ when $f$ is in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   **Data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** Fixed are a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime q`). Write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` and let `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` be the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((T))$ generated by the series `jqModC κ` $= T^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNum}$ and by its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion `jqNModC κ M'`. A finset $W$ of places of this field over $\kappa$ is given, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places in the sense of `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those $w$ which are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`, i.e. is a $j$-invariant such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hle` requires the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, that is, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q\bigl(\mathrm{qExpand}_{d}\, j_q : d \mid M'\bigr)$ is contained in the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^{2}M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^{2}M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, the requirement that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, compatibility of $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ with the residue map of $A$, existence for each nonzero $f$ of a constant scaling with nonzero residue, preservation of degrees by $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$, and compatibility of $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ with divisors of elements with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, this image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, viewed as a place.
--
--   **The small field and its local hypotheses.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ is given together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$. Write $A_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` of $k_0$ induced by $A$. Four hypotheses concern $A_0$: it is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), and its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`). The hypothesis `hκ` requires that every $a \in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary level.** A prime $\ell'$ is given with $3 \le \ell'$, $\ell' \ne q$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$, together with $\xi \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity. The field $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((T))/k_0$, and `hKℓ` identifies it with `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M'))`, the $k_0$-subfield of $k_0((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^{2}M'$, where now $H$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^{2}M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^{\times}$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$. Algebra and scalar-tower instances make $K_\ell$ an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K_\ell$. An element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is given whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `jq`, and $j_\ell \ne 0$.
--
--   Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥Kℓ jℓ` for the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the elements integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and `jChartFin` for $j_\ell$ regarded as an element of $C$. A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ is given (`hy`) containing the image of $\pi_0$ under $A_0 \to C$ (`hϖy`), and satisfying `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   **The condition that $y$ lies over $s$.** The hypothesis `hover` states: for every $g \in \mathbb Q((T))$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that (i) for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` being $\ge 0$ forces $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$ to be $\ge 0$, and (ii) the $R_0$-residue of the image of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$; then, whenever $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0,\ell'}(\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{k_0}\, g)$ lies in $K_\ell$ and the element of $K_\ell$ so obtained lies in $C$, and whenever $c \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and its residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of the image of $g$, the difference of that element of $C$ and the image of $c$ under $A_0 \to C$ lies in $y$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $G$ be the set of $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ for which there exists $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ (q*ℓ') ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M') γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ`; the latter predicate says that for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero associated Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of $\tau(x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/m \\ m\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   The assertion is the equality of natural cardinalities
--   $$\#G = \#X \cdot \#\mathrm{Stab},$$
--   where $X$ is the set of ideals $y'$ of $C$ that are maximal, contain the image of $\pi_0$ under $A_0 \to C$, and satisfy the same lying-over-$s$ condition as `hover` with $y'$ in place of $y$ (the supersingularity condition `hss` is not imposed on $y'$), and $\mathrm{Stab}$ is the set of $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ which belong to $G$ (the same existential condition on $\gamma$) and satisfy: for every $b \in C$ such that $\tau(b)$ again lies in $C$, one has $b \in y$ if and only if $\tau(b) \in y$.
--
--   This is the orbit–stabiliser count for the finite group of $k_0$-automorphisms of the auxiliary-level function field $K_\ell$ attached to elements of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, acting on the maximal ideals of the $j$-finite chart algebra that lie in the special fibre and over a fixed supersingular place $s$: the number of such automorphisms equals the number of such points times the number of those fixing the chosen point $y$ setwise. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace) in the comparison of stabiliser groups with automorphism groups at supersingular points of the reduction of the modular curve at $q$.
-- source:
